completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Describe the bug**\r\nlibsodium is missing a #define when built on macos.  The #define HAVE_SYSCONF controls how libsodium determines the page_size used in memory allocations.  This is in src/libsodium/sodium/utils.c, in the _alloc_aligned function.  When it is missing, the incorrect page_size is used.  This causes an assertion failure in src/libsodium/sodium/utils.c, in the _sodium_malloc function.\r\n\r\n**Environment**\r\n- OS: MacOS\r\n- Compiler: clang\r\n\r\n**To Reproduce**\r\nSteps to reproduce the behavior:\r\nBuild and use libsodium in an application.  The assert is triggered the first time the application attempts to allocate memory with libsodium.\r\n\r\n**Expected behavior**\r\nNo assertion when allocating memory.\r\n\r\n**Failure logs**\r\nAssertion failed: (_unprotected_ptr_from_user_ptr(user_ptr) == unprotected_ptr), function _sodium_malloc, file utils.c, line 629.\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\nThis can be fixed by adding\r\nsodium_check_func(sysconf HAVE_SYSCONF)\r\nto CMakeLists.txt in the port\r\n\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"vicroms","id":3526662,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MjY2NjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3526662?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vicroms","html_url":"https://github.com/vicroms","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vicroms/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vicroms/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vicroms/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vicroms/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vicroms/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vicroms/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vicroms/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vicroms/events{/privacy}","received_events_url